      "blocks": {
        "richtext_NhMgTp": {
          "type": "richtext",
          "settings": {
            "content": "<h6>Personality and emotional functioning evaluations are designed to provide a deeper understanding of how a person experiences themselves, relates to others, manages emotions, copes with stress, and responds to life circumstances. These evaluations can be especially helpful when symptoms feel complex, longstanding, confusing, or difficult to explain through a brief clinical conversation alone.</h6><h6>At Center for Balanced Living, these evaluations are completed with care, clinical depth, and respect for the whole person. The goal is not to reduce someone to a diagnosis, but to better understand the patterns that may be shaping their distress, relationships, coping style, and treatment needs.</h6>"
          }
        }
      },
